  "details": "- My left: Normal spawning particle\n\n- My right: Particle spawning through a \"broken sub-emitter\" (buffer particle)\n\nOnly I see this problem in the mirror. Nobody sees this in the mirror or normaly. This problem also doesn't appear in Unity itself.\n\nThis way of constructing particles is often used when shooting projectiles from a weapon. This is to prevent the previous projectile(s) from dissapearing, once a new one is spawned.\n\nThis has never been an problem up until now all of a sudden.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/I5QiXsla8qc",
